{"entity":"story","version":1,"id":"ekr-cli","revision":1,"type":"aep.entity.create/v1","from_state":null,"to_state":"draft","changed":{"body":"## Context\n\nDesign § 70 names the runtime's controlled interface: snapshot, ingest, propose, validate, commit,\nmaintain. P1 exposes the kernel half as the `ekr` binary so the epic's exit evidence — the § 65\nretraction example — can run end to end from a shell and a conformance suite can drive it.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nAn integration test drives the § 65 example through the binary — `seed`, `propose` Alice\n`CEO_OF` Acme, `validate`, `commit`, `propose` Bob with Alice's `valid_to`, `validate`, `commit`,\n`snapshot --valid-at` before and after 2026-03-12 — and the two snapshots name Alice and Bob\nrespectively with exit 0 at every step.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `crates/ekr/src/main.rs` — clap derive: `seed`, `propose`, `validate`, `commit`, `snapshot`,\n  `explain`, each with `--store <path>` and JSON on stdin/stdout, wire names from\n  `systems/ekr/domains/kernel.yaml`\n- `crates/ekr/src/cli/{seed,propose,validate,commit,snapshot,explain}.rs`\n- `crates/ekr/src/exit.rs` — exit codes: 0 outcome, 2 refusal by name, 1 fault\n- `crates/ekr/tests/retraction_example.rs`\n- `crates/ekr/tests/fixtures/` — the § 65 seed and transactions\n\n## Notes\n\nDepends on `story:seed-and-explain` and `story:eventlog-store`. A refusal (an error outcome in\nthe ESS domain) is exit 2 with the error name on stderr, so a driver can tell it from a fault.\n`ingest` and `maintain` are P2 and P6.\n","title":"The ekr binary: seed, propose, validate, commit, snapshot, explain"},"args":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"## Context\n\nDesign § 70 names the runtime's controlled interface: snapshot, ingest, propose, validate, commit,\nmaintain. P1 exposes the kernel half as the `ekr` binary so the epic's exit evidence — the § 65\nretraction example — can run end to end from a shell and a conformance suite can drive it.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nAn integration test drives the § 65 example through the binary — `seed`, `propose` Alice\n`CEO_OF` Acme, `validate`, `commit`, `propose` Bob with Alice's `valid_to`, `validate`, `commit`,\n`snapshot --valid-at` before and after 2026-03-12 — and the two snapshots name Alice and Bob\nrespectively with exit 0 at every step.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `crates/ekr/src/main.rs` — clap derive: `seed`, `propose`, `validate`, `commit`, `snapshot`,\n  `explain`, each with `--store <path>` and JSON on stdin/stdout, wire names from\n  `systems/ekr/domains/kernel.yaml`\n- `crates/ekr/src/cli/{seed,propose,validate,commit,snapshot,explain}.rs`\n- `crates/ekr/src/exit.rs` — exit codes: 0 outcome, 2 refusal by name, 1 fault\n- `crates/ekr/tests/retraction_example.rs`\n- `crates/ekr/tests/fixtures/` — the § 65 seed and transactions\n\n## Notes\n\nDepends on `story:seed-and-explain` and `story:eventlog-store`. A refusal (an error outcome in\nthe ESS domain) is exit 2 with the error name on stderr, so a driver can tell it from a fault.\n`ingest` and `maintain` are P2 and P6.\n","status":"draft","title":"The ekr binary: seed, propose, validate, commit, snapshot, explain"},"entity_type":"aep.story/v1","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/ekr-cli"},"payload":{"actor":"agent:claude","at":1789955946033,"causation":"cmd-new-story-ekr-cli","change":{"change":"created","status":"draft"},"correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","event_id":"story:ekr-cli@1#0~d5672affccbc2588","executor":null,"recorded_at":"2026-09-21T01:59:06Z"}}